def query_admin_infomodel(**kwargs):
    """
    * ADMIN *

    _*Query Admin Infomodel*_  Run query against InfoModel and return its result.Keyword will
       wait until the result is successful or timeout seconds pass.

    *Usage*:
    Query Admin Infomodel  <query>   <api_version>   <timeout>   <alias>   <extended_result=False>
        <allow_negative_result>    <str_format>

    *Parameters:*
    | *Arguments* | *Default* | *Comments* | *Config Ref* |
    | query  | Mandatory | Query expression on InfoModel. |  |
    | api_version | v1 | Query api version. Currently available api version is "v1" |  |
    | timeout | 10 | Timeout value |  |
    | dut | bts |  Section Name in Testline Config  | `testline_config` |
    | alias | default | Name of execution context |  |
    | extend_result | False | Extend result with additional data like query data timestamp |  |
    | allow_negative_result | False | Allow negative query result to be returned instead of |  |
    |   |   |   | InfoModelQueryTimeoutException |  |
    | *str_format* | True | is used only for query = "get param". Returns result if string format |  |
    |   |   | is True and result dictionary has one key else dictionary is returned |  |

    *Note*:
    Keyword performs exactly same as what Query Infomodel keyword of UTE's ute_admin_infomodel
        library does. In addition to it this keyword performs another operation "get param".
    Details on queries of UTE library's Keyword Query Infomodel is present in the link :
    http://doc.ute.inside.nsn.com/packages/ute_admin_infomodel/interfaces/ute_admin_infomodel.html#query-infomodel .
    Details on query "get param is present below.

    | *Query*  | *Syntax* | *description* |
    | *get param* | get param DIST_NAME:PARAMETER1:PARAMETER2:PARAMETER3 | keyword is used to get |
    |   |   | a parameter from bts. If value of PARAMETER1 for DIST_NAME contains a dictionary, then |
    |   |   | PARAMETER2 is fetched from it. Similarly, PARAMETER3 is fetched if value of PARAMETER2 is a |
    |   |   | dictionary. |

    DIST_NAME supports regular expression. To know how to use regular expression in DIST_NAME,
    check the link
    http://doc.ute.inside.nsn.com/packages/ute_admin_infomodel/interfaces/ute_admin_infomodel.html#query-infomodel

    *Example*
    | *keyword*  | *query* | *timeout* | *alias* | *extend_result* | *allow_negative_result* | *str_format* |
    | Query Admin Infomodel  | query=get param /MRBTS-1/RAT-1/BTS_L-1/BTS_CONF-1/NP-5/SCF-1/ | | | | | |
    |  | MRBTS_A-3263/LNBTS_A-3263/TRSNW_A-0:cPlane:ipV4AddressDN1:localIpAddr* | | | | | |
    | Query Admin Infomodel  | query=get param /MRBTS-1/RAT-1/BTS_L-1/BTS_CONF-1/NP-5/SCF-1/ | | | | | |
    |  | MRBTS_A-3263/LNBTS_A-3263/TRSNW_A-*:cPlane:ipV4AddressDN1:localIpAddr | timeout=30 | alias=default | | | |
    |  |  |  |  | extend_result=${False} | allow_negetive_result=${False} | str_format=${False} |
    | Query Admin Infomodel  | query=get list /MRBTS-1/RAT-1/BTS_L-1/BTS_CONF-1/NP-5/SCF-1/| | | | | |
    |  | MRBTS_A-3263/LNBTS_A-3263/TRSNW_A-*  | timeout=30 | alias=default | | | |
    |  |  |  |  | extend_result=${False} | allow_negetive_result=${False} | |

    * BTSSM *
        Implementation Not available

    """

    return OamFactory().get_instance(kwargs.get("dut", "bts")).query_admin_infomodel(**kwargs)


